# Help
help_title = Help
help_tools = Tools
help_button_tip = Help and documentation
help_tab_overview = Overview
help_tab_usage = Usage
help_tab_settings = Settings
help_tab_limitations = Limitations
help_disk_usage_overview_heading = What Disk Usage shows
help_disk_usage_overview_what = Disk Usage shows which folders and files take the most space. Every file and folder is drawn as a shape whose area is proportional to its size, so the biggest space consumers are visible at a glance.
help_disk_usage_overview_views = There are two views. Treemap draws nested rectangles. Rings draws concentric rings, with the scanned folder in the middle and its subfolders in the rings around it.
help_disk_usage_overview_colors = Colors show the type of a file, for example audio, video, images or archives. Folders have a color of their own.
help_disk_usage_usage_heading = Working with the chart
help_disk_usage_usage_start = Add folders to Included Paths in the bottom panel and press Scan. The chart appears when the scan is finished.
help_disk_usage_usage_hover = Hover over a shape to see the name, size and type of the item.
help_disk_usage_usage_select = Click a shape to select it. The details of the selected item are shown below the chart.
help_disk_usage_usage_open = Double click a shape to open the item in the system file manager or default application.
help_disk_usage_usage_scroll = Scroll up to zoom one level into the selected folder, it works when an item is selected. Scroll down to zoom out by one level. The Zoom out button does the same.
help_disk_usage_usage_rings = In the Rings view a list of folders is shown on the left, it can be expanded, and the center of the rings shows the size and the name of the folder that is zoomed.
help_disk_usage_usage_menu = Right click a shape to open the menu: open the item or its parent folder, copy its path or use Move to trash. For now Move to trash only removes the item from the chart, the file stays on the disk.
help_disk_usage_usage_filters = The type icons above the chart hide or show a file type, and the icon with borders turns on nested borders. The Levels slider, available in the Rings view, sets how many levels of folders are drawn, from 2 to 8 and 6 by default.
help_disk_usage_settings_heading = Options of the tool
help_disk_usage_settings_where = These options are available after clicking the tool settings button in the left panel.
help_disk_usage_settings_excluded_items = Ignore excluded items: on by default, so the excluded items patterns from the settings are not applied and hidden folders, caches and node_modules are counted. Untick it to skip them, the total then can be lower than the real disk usage.
help_disk_usage_settings_excluded_folders = Ignore excluded folders: measures also the folders from Excluded Paths in the bottom panel.
help_disk_usage_settings_detection = File type detection: files are recognized by extension. Files with an unknown extension can also be recognized by reading their beginning, by default only for files of at least 1 MiB, which is fast and covers most of the used space, or for all files, which is much slower.
help_disk_usage_settings_detail = Detail: Group entries smaller than merges entries that are a smaller share of their folder than the chosen one, from 1/100 to 1/10000000 and 1/1000000 by default. Smallest entry shown hides entries narrower than 1 to 10 pixels. Folders narrower than this are one block, from 0 to 60 pixels, where 0 turns it off. Showing more entries gives a more precise chart, but it takes longer to draw. Changes are applied immediately.
help_disk_usage_settings_not_saved = The options of Disk Usage are not saved in presets and are restored to their defaults after restarting the application.
help_disk_usage_limits_heading = Good to know
help_disk_usage_limits_symlinks = Symbolic links are not followed and have a size of zero. Hard links are counted once for every name.
help_disk_usage_limits_small = Very small entries are grouped into one block, because they would be too small to see.
help_disk_usage_limits_total = The total is the sum of the sizes of the files found by the scan, not of the space allocated on the disk. It can differ from the usage reported by the system, for example because of excluded folders, other filesystems or files that cannot be read.
help_disk_usage_limits_changes = The chart shows the state from the moment of the scan. Files changed later are not reflected until the next scan.
help_section_getting_started = Getting started
help_tab_quick_start = Quick start
help_getting_started_quick_start_h1 = Scanning in a few steps
help_getting_started_quick_start_b2 = Choose a tool in the left panel.
help_getting_started_quick_start_b3 = Add the folders to search in the Included Paths list in the bottom panel. Folders listed in Excluded Paths are skipped.
help_getting_started_quick_start_b4 = Press Scan and wait for the results. A scan only reads files, it never changes them.
help_getting_started_quick_start_b5 = Review the results, check the items you want with the checkboxes in the first column and use the action buttons, for example Delete or Move.
help_getting_started_quick_start_p6 = The gear icon under the tool list opens the general settings. The button on the right of it, when visible, opens the options of the currently selected tool.
help_getting_started_quick_start_p7 = Results are only suggestions, so check them before deleting anything. Moving files to the trash instead of deleting them permanently lets you undo a mistake.
help_getting_started_quick_start_p8 = Krokiet is the main graphical frontend of Czkawka. The same scanning engine is used by the command line tool czkawka_cli. The application does not use the Internet: there is no telemetry and no update checking.
help_tab_interface = Interface
help_getting_started_interface_h1 = Main window
help_getting_started_interface_b2 = Left panel: the list of tools. Clicking the logo opens the About page, the gear opens the settings, and the button with the cogs, shown only for tools that have options, opens a popup with the options of the selected tool. The small arrow in the top left corner collapses the whole panel, and the question mark near the logo opens this help.
help_getting_started_interface_b3 = Results area: found items are shown as rows. Bold rows are headers of groups, for example of a set of identical files.
help_getting_started_interface_b4 = Action bar: the Scan and Stop buttons, selection helpers and action buttons. Select, Save and Sort are available only when there are results and no scan is running. Move, Delete, Trash and the other actions that change files need at least one checked row.
help_getting_started_interface_b5 = Status line: shows the state of the scan or a short summary of the results.
help_getting_started_interface_b6 = Bottom panel: the folder button on the right side of the action bar shows the directory panel with Included Paths on the left and Excluded Paths on the right. The info button next to it shows the error log with messages collected during the scan. Both use the same place, clicking the active button hides the panel.
help_getting_started_interface_b7 = Preview: a picture of the highlighted row is shown on the right in Similar Images and Duplicate Files, if the image preview is enabled in the settings, and a video thumbnail in Similar Videos and Video Optimizer, if the thumbnail preview is enabled. The preview is hidden when several rows are highlighted. The splitter between the list and the preview can be dragged.
help_getting_started_interface_h8 = Paths
help_getting_started_interface_p9 = Included paths are scanned, excluded paths are skipped. Use the buttons above each list to add a folder, add a file or type a path manually. Typing a path is the easiest way to add a network share on Windows.
help_getting_started_interface_p10 = Every path has a button that removes it from the list. Double click on a path opens it and right click opens its parent folder.
help_getting_started_interface_p11 = The Ref checkbox next to an included path makes it a reference folder, see the Selecting and actions page.
help_tab_results = Results
help_getting_started_results_h1 = Highlighted and checked rows
help_getting_started_results_p2 = Every row has two separate states. A highlighted row is the one you point at, and a checked row is marked with the checkbox in the first column. Actions such as Delete or Move work on the checked rows. Clicking a row only highlights it, it never checks it.
help_getting_started_results_b3 = Click highlights a row and shows its preview. Ctrl+click adds or removes a single row from the highlighted ones, Shift+click highlights a range.
help_getting_started_results_b4 = Check rows with the checkboxes, with the Space key on the highlighted rows, or with the Select button.
help_getting_started_results_b5 = Double click a row to open the file in the default application.
help_getting_started_results_h6 = Context menu
help_getting_started_results_p7 = Right click highlights a row and opens a menu. It is not available on group headers.
help_getting_started_results_b8 = Open Item and Open Parent Folder.
help_getting_started_results_b9 = Remove from Results hides the row, and Remove All from Folder hides all rows from the folder of the row, also with subfolders in the recursive variant. The files stay on the disk.
help_getting_started_results_b10 = Select All from Folder, also recursive, checks all rows from that folder. In tools with groups one item of each group stays unchecked.
help_getting_started_results_b11 = Exclude Parent Folder and Exclude Item add the path to Excluded Paths and remove the matching rows from the list.
help_getting_started_results_b12 = Rename, which is useful for a single file, and Copy File Name, Copy Parent Folder and Copy Full Path.
help_getting_started_results_p13 = Rows from reference folders are protected from the removing, excluding and selecting entries.
help_getting_started_results_h14 = Sorting and columns
help_getting_started_results_b15 = Click a column header to sort by it. The first click sorts descending, the next ones change the direction. The header of the checkbox column sorts by the checked state.
help_getting_started_results_b16 = The Sort button opens a popup with sorting by the full name, sorting by focus, which moves the highlighted rows to the top, and reversing the order.
help_getting_started_results_b17 = Drag the dividers of the column headers to change the width of the columns. If some columns are not visible, use the horizontal scrollbar below the list.
help_section_selection = Selecting and actions
help_tab_selecting = Selecting
help_selection_selecting_h1 = Checking results
help_selection_selecting_p2 = Actions such as Delete, Move or Trash are applied to the checked rows. Check them with their checkboxes, with Space, or with the Select button, which opens a popup with ready to use modes. The modes depend on the tool.
help_selection_selecting_b3 = Select all, Unselect all, Invert selection and Custom are available in every tool.
help_selection_selecting_b4 = In Duplicate Files, Similar Images, Similar Videos and Music Duplicates there are also modes that work on each group: one oldest, newest, biggest or smallest file, all files except the oldest, newest, biggest or smallest, the shortest or the longest path and Invert selection in each group. Similar Images adds variants based on the resolution. Some of the modes can be hidden in the settings.
help_selection_selecting_p5 = The modes that choose one file or all except one always leave one file of the group unchecked. Select all and the inverting modes can check all files of a group, so the delete and trash popups tell how many groups would lose all their files.
help_selection_selecting_h6 = Custom selection
help_selection_selecting_p7 = Custom checks or unchecks rows by the values of the columns, for example the full path, the file name, the path, the size or the date. The columns that you enable must all match.
help_selection_selecting_b8 = Text columns use patterns with * as a wildcard. A pattern without * must match the whole value, and without a * at the beginning or at the end the pattern is anchored there. For example *.flac matches FLAC files and C:\Users\name\Desktop* matches everything in that folder.
help_selection_selecting_b9 = Number columns accept the operators >=, <=, >, < and =. The size is entered in KB.
help_selection_selecting_b10 = Dates are entered as DD-MM-YYYY or YYYY-MM-DD, optionally followed by a time HH:MM:SS.
help_selection_selecting_b11 = The Select button adds checks and the Unselect button removes them from the matching rows.
help_selection_selecting_b12 = The option to select all items except one in each group is on by default and exists only in tools with groups. It is switched off automatically when reference folders were used.
help_selection_selecting_b13 = The options Case sensitive and Save and restore filter data are also available.
help_selection_selecting_p14 = To check everything except one folder, check that folder with Custom and then invert the selection, or mark the folder as a reference folder.
help_tab_actions = Actions
help_selection_actions_h1 = What the buttons do
help_selection_actions_b2 = Delete: permanently removes the checked files. This cannot be undone. The popup shows how many items will be removed.
help_selection_actions_b3 = Trash: moves the checked files to the system trash, so they can be restored. It may fail on network shares and on drives without a trash folder, then use Delete.
help_selection_actions_b4 = Move: moves the checked files to a chosen folder. On the same drive it is instant, between drives the files are copied and then removed, which can take long. The popup can also copy instead of move, keep the folder structure and rename files on a name conflict instead of skipping them.
help_selection_actions_b5 = Hardlink and Softlink are available in Duplicate Files, Similar Images, Similar Videos and Music Duplicates. In a group with a reference file the links point to it. Otherwise the first checked file is kept and the other checked files of the group are replaced with links to it, so check at least two files in a group.
help_selection_actions_b6 = A hard link makes all names share the same data, so it takes the space only once. It works only inside one drive. On Windows a symbolic link needs administrator rights or enabled Developer Mode.
help_selection_actions_b7 = Save: asks for a folder and writes the results to three files there, a text file and a pretty and a compact JSON file. Saved results cannot be loaded back, a new scan is needed.
help_selection_actions_b8 = Rename is available in Bad Extensions and Bad Names, Optimize in Video Optimizer, Clean in Exif Remover and Compare in Similar Images.
help_selection_actions_p9 = Do not hardlink system or application files. A change of one name would then change every name. Add system folders like C:\Windows or /usr to the excluded paths before scanning.
help_tab_reference = Reference folders
help_selection_reference_h1 = Protecting your originals
help_selection_reference_p2 = A reference folder is scanned, but its files can never be checked or changed. They are shown only as the originals that the other files were compared with. Reference folders work in tools with groups: Duplicate Files, Similar Images, Similar Videos and Music Duplicates.
help_selection_reference_p3 = Check the Ref checkbox next to an included path to make it a reference folder. Typical use: add your curated library as a reference, add the downloads folder as a normal path, scan, check all rows and delete. Only the copies outside the library are removed.
help_selection_reference_p4 = Only groups that contain a file from a reference folder are shown. A group made only of files from normal folders, or only from reference folders, is hidden. In a group the reference file is shown in the header row, only one file per group.
help_selection_reference_p5 = If all included paths are marked as reference, the scan does not start.
help_section_settings = Settings
help_tab_filters = Filters
help_settings_filters_h1 = Scan filters
help_settings_filters_p2 = The filters are in Settings, not in the directory panel. They apply to all tools.
help_settings_filters_b3 = Allowed extensions: leave empty to scan all files or enter a list like jpg,png. The keywords image, video, music and text expand to the matching extensions.
help_settings_filters_b4 = Excluded extensions: extensions that are skipped.
help_settings_filters_b5 = Excluded items: comma separated wildcard patterns matched against the whole path, for example */tmp*,*/.git/*. Every pattern must contain *. The keyword DEFAULT inserts the default patterns. The defaults skip the trash, .git, node_modules, caches and on Linux the hidden folders in /home.
help_settings_filters_b6 = File size: the minimal and the maximal size of scanned files, in KB.
help_settings_filters_b7 = Recursive search: scan the subfolders too.
help_settings_filters_b8 = Hide hard links: count files that share the same data only once. On by default.
help_settings_filters_h9 = Excluded paths or excluded items
help_settings_filters_p10 = Excluded paths are whole folders chosen in the directory panel. They are pre-filled with system folders such as /proc, /dev, /sys and /snap on Linux or C:\Windows on Windows. Excluded items are patterns, so they can skip a kind of folder everywhere, for example */@ea* for Synology metadata or */.fuse_hidden* for temporary files of FUSE filesystems.
help_tab_general = General
help_settings_general_h1 = General options
help_settings_general_b2 = Language: changes immediately, no restart is needed.
help_settings_general_b3 = Dark theme: changes immediately.
help_settings_general_b4 = Show only icons: hides the labels of the action buttons.
help_settings_general_b5 = Thread number: how many CPU threads the scans use, 0 means all. Needs a restart. Lower it to keep the computer responsive during big scans.
help_settings_general_b6 = Application scale: manual scale of the interface, useful on high resolution screens. It works only when Use manual application scale is checked, otherwise the scale is detected automatically. Needs a restart.
help_settings_general_b7 = Use cache: remembers the results of costly calculations, for example hashes, so repeated scans are much faster.
help_settings_general_b8 = Delete automatically outdated cache entries: checks at most once a week if the cached files still exist and are unchanged.
help_settings_general_b9 = Ignore other filesystems: on Linux, does not enter folders that are on other drives than the scanned folder. Off by default.
help_settings_general_b10 = Load window size at startup, play a sound and show a notification when a scan ends.
help_settings_general_b11 = The buttons for opening the configuration and the cache folder, and counters of the size of the cache, thumbnails and logs.
help_settings_general_p12 = The settings are saved when the application is closed normally. After a crash the changes made in that session are lost, except presets saved with their buttons.
help_tab_presets = Presets
help_settings_presets_h1 = Presets
help_settings_presets_p2 = A preset stores the included and excluded paths, the filters and the options of all tools. Switch between presets to keep, for example, one configuration for photos and another for backups. Language, theme, scale and window size are global and are not part of presets.
help_settings_presets_p3 = There are ten user presets and one reserved slot used for folders passed on the command line.
help_settings_presets_p4 = The presets are saved in files named config_preset_0.json to config_preset_10.json in the configuration folder, the number is one less than the number shown in the application. The global settings are in config_general.json. The preset buttons save, load and reset a preset immediately.
help_tab_files = Config and cache
help_settings_files_h1 = Where the files are stored
help_settings_files_b2 = Linux: configuration in ~/.config/krokiet and cache in ~/.cache/czkawka.
help_settings_files_b3 = macOS: configuration in ~/Library/Application Support/pl.Qarmin.Krokiet and cache in ~/Library/Caches/pl.Qarmin.Czkawka.
help_settings_files_b4 = Windows: configuration in %APPDATA%\Qarmin\Krokiet\config and cache in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Qarmin\Czkawka\cache.
help_settings_files_p5 = The cache is shared by Krokiet and the command line tool. It stores only metadata such as hashes, sizes and dates, so even a huge scan produces a cache of at most a few hundred megabytes.
help_settings_files_p6 = The Clean outdated cache button in the settings removes the entries of files that no longer exist or have changed. If results look wrong or the application crashes while loading the cache, delete the cache folder, the next scan rebuilds it.
help_settings_files_p7 = Do not run two instances of the same tool at the same time, because they can corrupt its cache. Different tools use different cache files.
help_settings_files_h8 = Portable mode
help_settings_files_p9 = Set the environment variables CZKAWKA_CONFIG_PATH and CZKAWKA_CACHE_PATH before starting the application to keep the configuration and the cache in a chosen folder, for example on a USB drive.
help_settings_files_p10 = The option to also save the cache as JSON makes it possible to inspect or edit it. The JSON file is read only when the binary cache file does not exist, so delete the binary file after editing the JSON.
help_section_shortcuts = Shortcuts
help_tab_shortcuts = Shortcuts
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_h1 = Result lists
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_p2 = The keys work when the list has the focus and a row was clicked before. They move the highlight and skip the headers of groups.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b3 = Up and Down arrows: move the highlight by one row. Hold Shift to extend the highlighted range.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b4 = Page Up and Page Down: move by a whole page.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b5 = Home and End: jump to the first or the last row.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b6 = Space: check or uncheck all highlighted rows.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b7 = Enter: open the current item.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b8 = Ctrl+A: highlight all rows. It does not check them, press Space afterwards to check them all.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_h9 = Mouse
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b10 = Click highlights a row, Ctrl+click adds or removes one row and Shift+click highlights a range.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b11 = Double click opens the item.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b12 = Right click opens a menu with actions for the row, for example opening the parent folder or excluding the item from further scans.
help_shortcuts_shortcuts_b13 = In Disk Usage the mouse wheel zooms the chart.
help_duplicate_files_overview_h1 = Finding identical files
help_duplicate_files_overview_p2 = Duplicate Files finds files with the same content, even if their names and locations differ. Files are grouped by size, then compared by a fast hash of the first and the last 4 KB of the file, and only the files that still match get a hash of the whole content. Smaller files are hashed whole at once.
help_duplicate_files_overview_p3 = Only hashes are compared, the files are not compared byte by byte. Candidates must have exactly the same size and the same Blake3 hash, so a false match is practically impossible.
help_duplicate_files_overview_p4 = Hard links are ignored by default, so one file with many names is not reported as duplicates, and symbolic links are never followed. The methods that compare only the size or the name do not read the files at all.
help_tab_options = Options
help_duplicate_files_options_h1 = Options of the tool
help_duplicate_files_options_b2 = Check method: Hash compares the content and is recommended. Size and Name compare only the size or the name and give many false results. Size and Name combines both.
help_duplicate_files_options_b3 = Hash type: Blake3 is the default and is both fast and strong. CRC32 and XXH3 are fast but not cryptographic. All three are good enough in practice.
help_duplicate_files_options_b4 = Case sensitive: matters only for the methods that compare names.
help_duplicate_files_options_b5 = Use prehash and the minimal sizes of cached files are in the general settings. The prehash stage always runs, the option controls only whether the partial hashes are saved in the cache. Files smaller than the minimal sizes are not stored in the cache, because reading them is cheaper than loading the cache.
help_duplicate_files_options_b6 = Image preview: shown in the general settings, it shows a preview of the highlighted image.
help_tab_tips = Tips
help_duplicate_files_tips_h1 = Good to know
help_duplicate_files_tips_b2 = No duplicates found: the default minimal file size is 16 KB, smaller files are skipped. Lower it in Settings, the value there is in KB. Tiny files are skipped on purpose, because they are often equal by coincidence and would bury the important results.
help_duplicate_files_tips_b3 = The counter of the full hash stage shows only the files that reached it. Files that differ in size or in the partial hash do not need a full hash, so the number is smaller than the number of scanned files.
help_duplicate_files_tips_b4 = Files from the trash should not be found, because the default excluded items skip them. If they appear, the list of excluded items was probably changed or cleared.
help_duplicate_files_tips_b5 = Scanning a hard disk is slow because of seeks. Keep the cache and the prehash enabled and scan smaller parts of the drive.
help_duplicate_files_tips_b6 = To keep the originals safe, mark the folder with them as a reference folder. Hardlink and Softlink are available in this tool.
help_duplicate_files_tips_b7 = Stop reacts between files, so a very big file can delay stopping for a while.
help_empty_folders_overview_h1 = Finding empty folders
help_empty_folders_overview_p2 = Empty Folders finds folders that contain no files. A folder that contains only other empty folders is empty too, and only the topmost folder of such a branch is listed. Deleting it removes the whole branch.
help_empty_folders_overview_p3 = A folder that contains any other entry, even a symbolic link, is not empty. A folder with an excluded subfolder or one that cannot be read is not empty either. The size and extension filters do not apply.
help_empty_folders_overview_p4 = The tool has no options. Use Delete or Move on the checked folders, or Trash to be able to restore them.
help_big_files_overview_h1 = Finding the biggest files
help_big_files_overview_p2 = Big Files lists the biggest or the smallest files in the scanned folders, which is a quick way to find what takes the most space.
help_big_files_overview_b3 = Method: The Biggest or The Smallest.
help_big_files_overview_b4 = Number of files: how many entries are shown, 50 by default.
help_big_files_overview_p5 = The global filters of the minimal and the maximal file size are ignored here, and files of 0 bytes are never listed.
help_big_files_overview_p6 = For a visual overview of the whole disk use Disk Usage. Big Files is better when you need a list that can be selected and processed.
help_empty_files_overview_h1 = Finding empty files
help_empty_files_overview_p2 = Empty Files finds files that have a size of 0 bytes. The options can extend the search to other files that carry no useful data.
help_empty_files_overview_b3 = Files filled with null bytes: also reports files that are not empty, but contain only zero bytes. Disabled by default.
help_empty_files_overview_b4 = Files filled with non-printable characters: also reports files in which every byte is not a visible ASCII character, so also files made only of bytes above 127, for example some text files in non-Latin alphabets. Disabled by default.
help_empty_files_overview_p5 = The global filters of the file size are ignored in this tool.
help_empty_files_overview_p6 = Some programs create empty files on purpose, for example lock files or markers, so check the results before deleting.
help_temporary_files_overview_h1 = Finding temporary files
help_temporary_files_overview_p2 = Temporary Files finds files whose names end with one of the entries of a list of typical temporary suffixes, like partial downloads, backups and cache files. The comparison ignores the case of letters.
help_temporary_files_overview_p3 = The list can be edited in the options of the tool and restored with the Reset button. The default list contains: #, thumbs.db, .bak, ~, .tmp, .temp, .ds_store, .crdownload, .part, .cache, .dmp, .download and .partial.
help_temporary_files_overview_p4 = The list must not be empty and the size filters do not apply. Files that look temporary can still be in use, so close other programs before deleting them.
help_similar_images_overview_h1 = Finding similar pictures
help_similar_images_overview_p2 = Similar Images finds pictures that look alike, even if they differ in size, quality, format or have small edits. Every image gets a short perceptual fingerprint, and images with close fingerprints are grouped.
help_similar_images_overview_p3 = The content is compared, not the file format, so a JPEG and a WebP of the same picture are grouped together. The orientation saved in EXIF is applied before the comparison.
help_similar_images_overview_p4 = Supported formats: JPEG, PNG, BMP, TIFF, WebP, TGA, Farbfeld, QOI, EXR, JXL and RAW files. HEIC needs a build with heif support and AVIF a build with avif support. GIF and ICO are not scanned. The optional libraw library only replaces the built in RAW decoder.
help_similar_images_overview_p5 = The algorithms ignore colors, so a black and white copy of a picture is found as similar to the original.
help_similar_images_options_h1 = Options of the tool
help_similar_images_options_b2 = Max difference: the maximal distance of the fingerprints, from 0 to 40 and 10 by default. Lower values are stricter. A fingerprint of hash size 8 has 64 bits, so 40 matches almost everything.
help_similar_images_options_b3 = Hash size: 8, 16, 32 or 64, 16 by default. A bigger fingerprint is more precise and gives fewer false matches, but needs a higher max difference to find re-encoded copies.
help_similar_images_options_b4 = Hash type: Mean (default, fastest and most permissive), Gradient, VertGradient, DoubleGradient, Median and BlockHash. Gradient types are more sensitive to structure, Median resists brightness changes and BlockHash does not resize the image.
help_similar_images_options_b5 = Resize algorithm: how the image is shrunk before hashing: Lanczos3 (default), Gaussian, CatmullRom, Triangle or Nearest.
help_similar_images_options_b6 = Geometric invariance: off by default, or also finds mirrored and flipped images, or additionally images rotated by 90, 180 and 270 degrees. It makes the scan slower.
help_similar_images_options_b7 = Ignore images with the same size or the same resolution: hides groups where all images have identical byte size or pixel dimensions.
help_similar_images_tips_h1 = Good to know
help_similar_images_tips_b2 = Known copies are not found: lower the minimal file size, which is 16 KB by default, raise the max difference, or try Gradient or DoubleGradient with hash size 32 or 64.
help_similar_images_tips_b3 = Too many unrelated pictures in a group: lower the max difference to 4 or 5 and raise the hash size. Large uniform areas like black borders make pictures look similar.
help_similar_images_tips_b4 = A good start for re-encoded or resized copies is Mean with hash size 16 and max difference between 8 and 10. For stricter matching use Gradient with size 32 and difference 4 or 5.
help_similar_images_tips_b5 = The Compare button opens a side by side view of the images from a group, with an overlay and a difference mode.
help_similar_images_tips_b6 = HEIC pictures are found only by builds with heif support, AVIF by builds with avif support.
help_similar_images_tips_b7 = Changing the hash size, the hash type, the resize algorithm or the geometric invariance needs the images to be hashed again, because they are part of the cache key. The image preview option is in the general settings.
help_similar_videos_overview_h1 = Finding similar videos
help_similar_videos_overview_p2 = Similar Videos samples frames from each video, computes their perceptual hashes and compares the sequences in short windows of time. It finds re-encoded or resized copies of the same material, and also a shorter clip that is a part of a longer video.
help_similar_videos_overview_p3 = The visual mode needs ffmpeg and ffprobe available in PATH. They are not bundled. Restart the application after installing them. The audio fingerprint mode does not need them, but the thumbnails do.
help_similar_videos_overview_b4 = Linux: sudo apt install ffmpeg or sudo pacman -S ffmpeg.
help_similar_videos_overview_b5 = macOS: brew install ffmpeg.
help_similar_videos_overview_b6 = Windows: install ffmpeg and add its folder to PATH, or place ffmpeg.exe next to the Krokiet executable.
help_similar_videos_overview_p7 = There is also an audio fingerprint mode that compares the sound of the videos. It is more demanding and is switched on in the options.
help_similar_videos_options_h1 = Options of the visual mode
help_similar_videos_options_p2 = A quick preset sets the values for you: Near-identical, Similar and Movies (long skip). Choose Custom to change them yourself, the sliders are shown only then.
help_similar_videos_options_b3 = Max difference: how different two videos can be, from 0 to 20, 15 by default. Lower is stricter.
help_similar_videos_options_b4 = Skip duration: the number of seconds skipped at the start, from 0 to 300 and 15 by default, to avoid intros and black openers. It is never more than 15 percent of the length of a video.
help_similar_videos_options_b5 = Video hash duration: the length of every sampled window, from 2 to 60 seconds and 10 by default.
help_similar_videos_options_b6 = Window count: how many places of the video are sampled, from 1 to 20 and 5 by default. More is more accurate and slower.
help_similar_videos_options_b7 = Duration tolerance: videos are compared only if their lengths differ by no more than this percentage, 20 by default.
help_similar_videos_options_b8 = Min matching windows: the share of windows that must agree to call two videos the same, from 20 to 100 percent and 60 by default.
help_similar_videos_options_b9 = Subclip min match: the share of windows that must agree to find a shorter clip inside a longer video, 50 percent by default.
help_similar_videos_options_b10 = Letterbox crop detection, which is on by default, and ignoring videos with the same size or the same resolution.
help_similar_videos_options_h11 = Options of the audio mode
help_similar_videos_options_b12 = Presets: Identical videos, Clip in longer video and Similar content, or Custom with the similarity (80 percent by default), the length ratio (0.1), the minimal duration of a file (10 seconds) and the maximal audio difference (3).
help_similar_videos_tips_h1 = Good to know
help_similar_videos_tips_b2 = Nothing is found: raise the video hash duration and the window count, lower the skip duration, raise the max difference, lower the min matching windows or raise the duration tolerance.
help_similar_videos_tips_b3 = Too many false matches: lower the max difference. Common intros and outros can also cause them. Short videos are still compared, the windows are made smaller for them.
help_similar_videos_tips_b4 = Every video is processed only once. In the visual mode the cache depends on the skip duration, the hash duration, the crop detection and the window count, so changing them needs a new processing. Parameters of grouping, such as max difference, do not invalidate the cache.
help_similar_videos_tips_b5 = Thumbnails of the results are configured in the general settings: the position in the video, a grid of tiles instead of one picture and removing unused thumbnails older than 7 days.
help_music_duplicates_overview_h1 = Finding duplicate music
help_music_duplicates_overview_p2 = Music Duplicates finds the same songs stored in different files or in different quality. There are two ways of comparing them.
help_music_duplicates_overview_b3 = Tags: compares the tags saved in the files. Title and artist are compared by default. You can also compare bitrate, genre, year and length. All selected tags must match. The approximate comparison works only for the title and the artist, it ignores the case, the text in brackets and the punctuation. Files with an empty tag are not grouped by it.
help_music_duplicates_overview_b4 = Fingerprint: compares the sound itself, so it finds the same recording even with missing or different tags. The option to compare within groups of similar titles is off by default. The max difference is from 0 to 10 and 3 by default, and the minimal duration of the compared fragment is from 0 to 180 seconds and 5 by default.
help_music_duplicates_overview_p5 = Fingerprints need more time than tags.
help_broken_files_overview_h1 = Finding damaged files
help_broken_files_overview_p2 = Broken Files checks if the files can be opened by a library for their type. Files that fail are probably corrupted or truncated.
help_broken_files_overview_p3 = Choose the checked types in the options. Enabled by default: audio, PDF, archives, images, fonts and markup (JSON, XML, TOML, YAML and SVG). Disabled by default: video.
help_broken_files_overview_b4 = The files are chosen by their extension, and a video is checked only if one of the two video options is enabled.
help_broken_files_overview_b5 = Video (ffprobe) is a quick check of the header and needs ffmpeg.
help_broken_files_overview_b6 = Video (ffmpeg) decodes the whole file, which is very slow, and needs ffmpeg.
help_broken_files_overview_p7 = The libraries can report problems in files that work fine. For example the message about an invalid main_data offset in MP3 files is caused by a very strict decoder and most players play such files. Check the files before deleting them.
help_invalid_symlinks_overview_h1 = Finding broken links
help_invalid_symlinks_overview_p2 = Invalid Symlinks finds symbolic links that point to a missing target or form an endless loop. A link in the middle of a chain that is not a link itself is skipped. The tool has no options.
help_invalid_symlinks_overview_p3 = Deleting a result removes the link only. In all other tools symbolic links are not followed and not scanned.
help_bad_extensions_overview_h1 = Finding wrong extensions
help_bad_extensions_overview_p2 = Bad Extensions compares the extension of a file with its real type, which is detected from the first bytes of the content. The Proper Extension column shows what the file really is. The tool has no options, and some extensions are never reported.
help_bad_extensions_overview_p3 = Use the Rename button to apply the suggestion to the checked files, or the Rename entry in the context menu for one file. The rename is skipped with a warning if a file with the new name already exists.
help_bad_extensions_overview_p4 = Many formats share the same beginning, so the detection is not always unambiguous. ZIP based files like docx, xlsx, jar, apk and epub all look like ZIP archives, and old doc, xls and ppt files share one container. In such cases the tool can only report the family of the format, so check the results before renaming.
help_bad_names_overview_h1 = Finding problematic names
help_bad_names_overview_p2 = Bad Names finds files whose names can cause problems, for example when moving them between systems, and suggests a corrected name. Use Rename to apply it, a file is not renamed if the new name already exists.
help_bad_names_overview_b3 = Uppercase extension, for example .JPG. On by default.
help_bad_names_overview_b4 = Emoji in the name. On by default.
help_bad_names_overview_b5 = Spaces at the beginning or at the end of the name. On by default.
help_bad_names_overview_b6 = Non-ASCII characters like ą, ć or ñ, replaced with ASCII equivalents, and the characters * ? [ ] are removed. On by default.
help_bad_names_overview_b7 = Limited charset: allows only ASCII letters, digits and the characters that you list, by default a space and the characters _ . , - ( ) [ ] ! ' and the quotation mark. Letters are first replaced with their ASCII equivalents and the rest is removed, in the name and in the extension. Off by default.
help_bad_names_overview_b8 = Duplicated characters, for example file---name: only repeated characters that are not letters or digits are merged. Off by default.
help_exif_remover_overview_h1 = Removing metadata from pictures
help_exif_remover_overview_p2 = Exif Remover finds images that contain EXIF metadata such as GPS position, the camera model or the date of creation. It is useful before sharing pictures.
help_exif_remover_overview_p3 = Press Clean to remove the metadata from the checked files. The list of ignored tags keeps the listed tags, separated by commas, using their exact names with the same case. By default it contains Orientation, so that pictures are not rotated. When the list is empty, all tags are removed.
help_exif_remover_overview_p4 = The Clean popup has the option Overwrite files, which is off by default. Without it the original stays untouched and a copy named name.czkawka_cleaned_exif.ext is created. When you overwrite, make a backup of pictures that you cannot afford to lose.
help_exif_remover_overview_p5 = Only the formats supported by the cleaning library are handled, for example JPEG, PNG, TIFF, WebP, JXL and HEIF.
help_video_optimizer_overview_h1 = Making videos smaller
help_video_optimizer_overview_p2 = Video Optimizer finds videos that can be made smaller and processes them with ffmpeg. It works in one of two modes.
help_video_optimizer_overview_b3 = Crop: finds videos with black bars or with a static area and cuts them off. Black Bars is the default type, with a threshold of the black pixels (20 by default) and a minimal percentage of the bars (90 by default). The second type is Static Content.
help_video_optimizer_overview_b4 = Transcode, the default mode: re-encodes videos to a better codec. Videos that already use the codecs from the excluded list, by default h265, hevc, av1 and vp9, are skipped. The Reset button restores the list.
help_video_optimizer_overview_p5 = Press Optimize to open a popup with the output settings and to start the processing. For transcoding the popup offers the video codec, the hardware encoder, the CRF quality, noise reduction, limits of the size and of the frame rate, overwriting of files, and a custom ffmpeg command. The tool needs ffmpeg installed.
help_section_faq = FAQ
help_faq_general_q1 = Does the app delete files on its own?
help_faq_general_a2 = No. A scan only reads files. Nothing is deleted, moved or renamed until you choose an action and confirm it.
help_faq_general_q3 = Does the application use the Internet?
help_faq_general_a4 = No. It has no telemetry, no update checks and no networking code. Official downloads are only on the GitHub releases page and on crates.io.
help_faq_general_q5 = What is the difference between Czkawka, Krokiet and the CLI?
help_faq_general_a6 = All of them use the same scanning engine. Krokiet is the current graphical interface, the GTK version is deprecated and receives no new features, and czkawka_cli is the command line version for scripts.
help_faq_general_q7 = What is the license?
help_faq_general_a8 = The engine, the command line tool and the GTK version are MIT. Krokiet and Cedinia are GPL-3.0 as a whole, because they use Slint under its free license, but their own code is MIT. Images and audio are CC BY 4.0.
help_faq_general_q9 = Which build should I download?
help_faq_general_a10 = Take the krokiet build for your system with the default renderer. Use the other renderers only if the default one shows blurry text or crashes. Builds with heif, raw or avif in the name are needed only for those image formats. AppImage is no longer provided, and Snap and Flatpak are outdated.
help_faq_general_q11 = Which systems are supported?
help_faq_general_a12 = Windows 10 or newer, Linux like Ubuntu 22.04 or newer and macOS on Intel and Apple Silicon. Windows 7 and older are not supported.
help_faq_general_q13 = Is there a version for Android?
help_faq_general_a14 = Yes, Cedinia is an experimental Android application based on the same engine.
help_faq_general_q15 = Can I use a nightly build?
help_faq_general_a16 = Yes, builds of the newest code are published on the GitHub releases page under the Nightly tag. They contain new features and fixes, and also unknown bugs.
help_faq_general_q17 = Can I run two instances at once?
help_faq_general_a18 = Different tools can run at the same time, but never run the same tool twice, because the cache of that tool can be corrupted.
help_tab_scanning = Scanning
help_faq_scanning_q1 = Why are my identical files not found?
help_faq_scanning_a2 = Probably they are smaller than the minimal file size, which is 16 KB by default. Lower it in Settings, the value is in KB.
help_faq_scanning_q3 = Why are symbolic links not scanned?
help_faq_scanning_a4 = Symbolic links are never followed. This avoids counting the same data twice and endless loops. To scan a folder behind a link, add its real path.
help_faq_scanning_q5 = Are hard links reported as duplicates?
help_faq_scanning_a6 = No, not by default. Names that share the same data are counted once. Disable the option that hides hard links to see them.
help_faq_scanning_q7 = The scan looks frozen near the end and Stop does nothing.
help_faq_scanning_a8 = The work can be stopped only between files. A very big or slow file must be finished first. This is improved in some tools, for example in duplicates and similar videos.
help_faq_scanning_q9 = Why are there permission errors in the log?
help_faq_scanning_a10 = Some folders such as .ssh, /proc or C:\System Volume Information cannot be read by a normal user. The errors are harmless and the scan continues. Add such folders to the excluded paths to hide them.
help_faq_scanning_q11 = How do I scan a network share or an external drive?
help_faq_scanning_a12 = On Windows type the UNC path in the manual add field, or map the share to a drive letter. Add patterns like */@ea* for Synology or */.Spotlight* for macOS to the excluded items to skip system metadata.
help_faq_scanning_q13 = Scanning a hard disk is very slow.
help_faq_scanning_a14 = That is limited by the seek time of the disk. Keep the cache and prehash enabled and scan smaller folders at once.
help_faq_scanning_q15 = Why is the CPU used so much?
help_faq_scanning_a16 = Hashing and decoding use all cores, other stages mostly wait for the disk. Lower the thread number in Settings to limit it, a restart is needed.
help_faq_scanning_q17 = Can I scan a phone?
help_faq_scanning_a18 = Not through MTP, because it is not a normal filesystem. Mount the storage with a tool that exposes it as a folder, or copy the files to the computer.
help_faq_results_q1 = If I check everything and delete, are all copies removed?
help_faq_results_a2 = The modes that choose one file or all except one always leave one file per group. Select all and Invert can check every file of a group, and then the delete popup tells how many groups would lose all their files.
help_faq_results_q3 = How do I delete duplicates from one folder and keep the other?
help_faq_results_a4 = Mark the folder you want to keep as a reference folder, scan, select all and delete. Files from reference folders are never selected.
help_faq_results_q5 = Delete or Trash does nothing, or fails.
help_faq_results_a6 = Moving to the trash does not work on network shares and on drives without a trash folder, use Delete there. Also check if the parent folder is writable.
help_faq_results_q7 = Why is Move so slow?
help_faq_results_a8 = Inside one drive a move is instant. Between drives the file is copied and then removed.
help_faq_results_q9 = What does Hardlink do and can it break something?
help_faq_results_a10 = It replaces the checked duplicates with links to one kept file. It cannot join different drives, then an error is reported and the file stays untouched. Do not use it on system files.
help_faq_results_q11 = Can I load saved results back?
help_faq_results_a12 = No. Saving always writes a text file and two JSON files, which are for reading and for your own scripts. To see the results in the application, scan again.
help_faq_results_q13 = Bad Extensions suggests a strange extension.
help_faq_results_a14 = Many formats share the same beginning, for example docx, xlsx and jar are all ZIP files. The tool can only name the family of the format, so check before renaming.
help_faq_results_q15 = What are the .fuse_hidden files?
help_faq_results_a16 = They are created by the operating system when a file that is still open is deleted on a FUSE filesystem. They are not duplicates, add */.fuse_hidden* to the excluded items to skip them.
help_faq_results_q17 = Broken Files reports an MP3 with an invalid main_data offset.
help_faq_results_a18 = The decoder is very strict, and the file usually plays fine. You can keep it.
help_tab_troubleshooting = Troubleshooting
help_faq_troubleshooting_q1 = The window is black, empty or crashes.
help_faq_troubleshooting_a2 = Try another renderer. Start the build with all backends through its launcher scripts, or set SLINT_BACKEND=software before starting the application. Also update the graphics drivers.
help_faq_troubleshooting_q3 = The text is too small or too big.
help_faq_troubleshooting_a4 = Check Use manual application scale in Settings, set the application scale and restart the application. Without the checkbox the scale is detected automatically.
help_faq_troubleshooting_q5 = Similar Videos or Broken Files report that ffmpeg is missing.
help_faq_troubleshooting_a6 = Install ffmpeg so that ffmpeg and ffprobe are in PATH, and restart the application. On Windows ffmpeg.exe can be put next to the Krokiet executable.
help_faq_troubleshooting_q7 = HEIC, AVIF or RAW pictures are not found.
help_faq_troubleshooting_a8 = Use a build with the matching feature and install its library. Plain builds do not include HEIF and AVIF.
help_faq_troubleshooting_q9 = The antivirus reports Krokiet as a threat.
help_faq_troubleshooting_a10 = This is a known false positive of optimized Rust binaries. The files are built from open source code on a public CI. Allow the file or report it to the antivirus vendor.
help_faq_troubleshooting_q11 = Results look wrong or the application crashes while loading the cache.
help_faq_troubleshooting_a12 = Delete the cache folder, the next scan builds it again, a bit slower.
help_faq_troubleshooting_q13 = The interface is slow with a lot of text in the bottom panel.
help_faq_troubleshooting_a14 = A very long text in the bottom panel is slow to draw. Hide the panel, the list of the results itself is not affected.
help_faq_troubleshooting_q15 = Can I add folders by drag and drop?
help_faq_troubleshooting_a16 = Not yet, because the interface library does not support it. Use the add buttons or type the path.
help_faq_troubleshooting_q17 = Where can I read more?
help_faq_troubleshooting_a18 = In the instructions and the FAQ in the instructions folder of the repository, and on the GitHub page of the project, where you can also report problems.
